. ** panel unit roots (descriptive only): Harris-Tzavalis is the test whose asymptotics hol
> d
. ** for fixed T = 9; IPS / Fisher need T -> infinity. All are first-generation tests, so t
> he
. ** cross-sectional means are removed (demean) to soften the common-shock problem. Two-way
. ** FE with cluster SE does not rely on stationarity when N-asymptotics carry the inferenc
> e.
. local urvars y_ipm y_tpt y_gini y_p0 y_lnwage y_padr $invall

. local nv : word count `urvars'

. matrix UR = J(`nv', 4, .)

. matrix rownames UR = `urvars'

. matrix colnames UR = HT_p HT_trend_p IPS_p FisherADF_p

. local i = 0

. foreach v of local urvars {
  2.         local ++i
  3.         capture xtunitroot ht `v', demean
  4.         if _rc == 0 matrix UR[`i',1] = r(p)
  5.         capture xtunitroot ht `v', trend demean
  6.         if _rc == 0 matrix UR[`i',2] = r(p)
  7.         capture xtunitroot ips `v', demean
  8.         if _rc == 0 matrix UR[`i',3] = r(p_wtbar)
  9.         capture xtunitroot fisher `v', dfuller lags(0) demean
 10.         if _rc == 0 matrix UR[`i',4] = r(p_P)
 11. }

. display as text _n "panel unit-root tests, p-values (H0: unit root), cross-sectionally de
> meaned; HT suited to T = 9"

